    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d431">

                <pb facs="0609" n="323" xml:id="pg323"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 865.857/26</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Chargé in Germany</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Grew</hi>)<anchor n="1" xml:id="d431-f1"/>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1916-12-09T20:00:00-05:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">December 9, 1916, 8 p. m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>3655. Department advised that Italian S. S. <hi rendition="#italic">Palermo, en
                        route</hi> from New York to Genoa with cargo of horses, was torpedoed
                    without warning by submarine of unknown nationality 25 miles off Cape San
                    Sebastian, Spain, December 2, 11.40 a. m.; that no attempt was made to escape or
                    resist, and that there were on board 48 Americans, of whom one was drowned.</p>
                <p>Please bring this case to attention of Foreign Minister, with urgent request for
                    prompt investigation and report on sinking of this vessel.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Lansing</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d431-f1" n="1" type="source" xml:id="d431-f1-content">
                <p>The same to the Ambassador in Austria-Hungary, No. 1446.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
